@startuml v1-daemon
!theme plain
title v1: the daemon on the same core (socket, queue, events, session-host backend)

participant "Orchestrator\n(agent account)" as O
participant "curator-dispatcherd\n(cur-s-dispatch)" as D
participant "Session host\n(later)" as SH
participant "Supervisor\n(inside the daemon)" as S

O -> D : connect; peer UID from the kernel;\ncheck server identity; hello {versions: [1]}
O -> D : subscribe {my runs}
O -> D : dispatch {request_id, …}
D -> D : prepare; capacity: slots full
D --> O : queued {handle, position}
... a run ends, a slot frees ...
D -> D : provision (helper, broker) as in v0
alt session host present
  D -> SH : start and hold executor (host uses the launcher)
  SH --> D : events: started, exited
else no session host
  D -> S : supervise (sudo launcher → executor)
end
D --> O : event: running {run_id}
... 
D --> O : event: done {exit}
note over D
  drain: stop admitting, finish running work (operators)
  records written by v0 are reconciled and continued
end note
@enduml
